<title>UK: UK backdating of VAT claims to be limited to 3 yrs.</title>
<headline>UK backdating of VAT claims to be limited to 3 yrs.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>UK Chancellor of the Exchequer Kenneth Clarke said the right of the Customs service to claim underpaid tax would be restricted to backdating of three years.</p>
<p>&quot;I have...decided that Customs' right to claim underpaid tax, in cases where no fraud or malpractice is involved, should be restricted to three years&quot; Clarke told parliament in his budget speech.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
